ted once (10 until then) — 5 `tool_call` and 3 `command` lines in each, needles 0 under both builds (escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep/evidence/log-counts.md); the format is exercised by `mcp_log` at `RUST_LOG=trace` under both builds and in process by `stand_mcp_tools` in both layout modes (packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:537-540; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:48-273; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_mcp_tools.rs:222-394; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-mcp-surface/report.md); typed text is measured on the `escher-session` host since 2026-10-10-driver-cli — 0 occurrences of a typed sentinel, 0 id needles and 0 name needles on the host's stderr at `RUST_LOG=trace`, `host_log` green as `-p seven_guis` and as `--workspace` — it stays unmeasured on `seven_guis_native`, and it was first measured in process — `stand_act_spans` drives `type` through `Session::run` with the sink installed over a capture at `RUST_LOG=info` and reads 0 occurrences of the supplied texts, 0 of 36 ids and 0 of 8 names in each layout mode (obs-plan §8; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist/evidence/by-level.md, the in-process capture at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md); `escher-session`'s format, and its host role's empty stdout, are exercised by seven_guis' `host_binary` and, at `RUST_LOG=trace` with no id, no name and no typed text on stderr, by `host_log`; a command's stdout is its answer and nothing else — one line of JSON, no ESC byte, an accepted command's stderr empty with `RUST_LOG` unset — exercised by `cli_commands` (examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:22-253; examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs:63-75); the format and the drop are exercised by `telemetry_stdout_silent`, `telemetry_scrub`, `telemetry_panic_hook`, `telemetry_init_idempotent` and `telemetry_drop` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/telemetry_stdout_silent.rs:1-36; tests/blitz-tests/tests/telemetry_scrub.rs:1-61; tests/blitz-tes